          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "The Journey Beyond"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.448,
            0.775,
            0.516
          ],
          "content": "y Demonstrate the Tyndall effect using different colloids. Create a series of experiments showcasing how light scatters in colloids making the beam visible. Use laser pointers (**Safety first:** Use it under the supervision of an adult), flashlights, or other light sources for your demonstrations."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.517,
            0.774,
            0.567
          ],
          "content": "y Make crystals of different compounds (common salt, epsom salt, sugar, borax, nickel sulfate, etc.). Observe them under a magnifying glass or a microscope. Note down their colours and shapes."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.568,
            0.774,
            0.602
          ],
          "content": "y Do red leaves also contain green pigments? Investigate it using paper chromatography."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.603,
            0.774,
            0.653
          ],
          "content": "You can try chromatography to find the number of components present in a food colour (green, orange, yellow, etc.) or in coloured mouth fresheners (fennel seeds)."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.655,
            0.774,
            0.706
          ],
          "content": "y Design an educational game where players identify and apply separation techniques to different mixtures through interactive challenges and hands-on activities."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.706,
            0.775,
            0.757
          ],
          "content": "y If you are camping outdoors and running short on clean water, you can obtain clean water by distillation. Can you think of a set-up with the items available to you?"
        },
        {
